# Erik Satie, Gymnopedie No. 1, played by SYN-5.3's sequencer on the sampled
# CONCERT GRAND-16 (W1:PIANO2 1-2: the grand recorded at pp, mf, f, ff; key
# velocity picks the recording) while Music Notation (Main Menu K) follows
# it: two staves (right hand track 1, left hand track 2), D major, 3/4, four
# measures a screen; the screen turns its own pages during playback. All
# three voices on the mf recordings: melody 17 (top of mf), bass 13, chords 9
# (bottom of mf).
#
# W1-SAMPLES-FIX.IMG = W1-SAMPLES built with the patch transposition fix
# (PR #68, tools/sample_pitch.py), so the piano is in tune.
# W0-53-GYMNO.IMG = W0-53.IMG with the piece as W0:.SQ5DATA (docs/demo-video.md):
#   python3 tools/seq_record.py record out/scores/Erik_Satie_-_Gymnopedie_No.1.mxl \
#     --w0 out/images/W0-53.IMG --w1 out/images/W1-SAMPLES-FIX.IMG --catalog W1:PIANO2 \
#     --timbre 1-2 --slot 5 --beat-ms 870 --velocity 1/2=17,2/5=13,1/1=9,2/6=9 \
#     --sseq out/gymnopedie.sseq                                          # 69 BPM
#   python3 tools/seq_record.py install out/gymnopedie.sseq --w0 out/images/W0-53.IMG \
#     --slot 5 --out out/images/W0-53-GYMNO.IMG
# (--velocity: MusicXML staff/voice: 1/2 melody, 2/5 bass, 1/1 and 2/6 chords.)
# On the MiSTer: Synclavier-Gymnopedie.mgl (M23G core, these two images).
title: Satie - Gymnopedie No. 1 (CONCERT GRAND-16, Music Notation)
w0: W0-53-GYMNO.IMG
w1: W1-SAMPLES-FIX.IMG

button seqb                 # SEQUENCE + 5: W0:.SQ5DATA, with its CONCERT GRAND-16 tracks
button timb.5
wait 60                     # the four layers' sound files load into poly memory
type K                      # Music Notation
wait 12
type 2                      # Staves
key ENTER
wait 12
key DOWN
wait 1
type 4                      # Measures (a screen)
key ENTER
wait 12
key UP
wait 1
key RIGHT
wait 1
key RIGHT
wait 1
type 3/4                    # TimeSig
key ENTER
wait 12
key DOWN
wait 1
key DOWN
wait 1
key DOWN                    # staff 1: Key
wait 1
type D
key ENTER
wait 12
key DOWN                    # Clf (G)
wait 1
key DOWN                    # Res
wait 1
type =                      # staff 2: Key
wait 1
key UP
wait 1
key UP
wait 1
type D
key ENTER
wait 12
key DOWN                    # Clf
wait 1
type F
key ENTER
wait 12
record
wait 2
button start
wait 125
button stop
wait 2
